WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:06.62
This is journey thirty seven of Hewn, the software factory: configure protected

00:00:06.62 --> 00:00:07.91
service credentials.

00:00:07.91 --> 00:00:10.31
It is for the operator who runs Hewn.

00:00:10.31 --> 00:00:15.63
The model API key, the Magic Patterns token and the GitHub keys now live encrypted

00:00:15.63 --> 00:00:16.79
in a secret store.

00:00:16.79 --> 00:00:18.74
Settings show only references.

00:00:18.74 --> 00:00:24.18
Anything that would leak one into a log, an event or a pull request says three stars

00:00:24.18 --> 00:00:24.70
instead.

00:00:24.70 --> 00:00:29.23
And a run's workspace takes its credentials with it when the run ends.

00:00:30.38 --> 00:00:32.94
The requirements come in two parts.

00:00:32.94 --> 00:00:36.09
Secrets: credentials are encrypted at rest,

00:00:36.09 --> 00:00:40.70
in a cloud key vault in the cloud and the OS key store locally,

00:00:40.70 --> 00:00:43.11
and no API response contains one.

00:00:43.11 --> 00:00:48.67
A log line, event or pull request body holding a stored secret, or a GitHub,

00:00:48.67 --> 00:00:54.59
Anthropic or Azure token, is redacted to three stars before it is stored or sent.

00:00:54.59 --> 00:00:59.79
And credentials written into a workspace are deleted when the run ends.

00:00:59.79 --> 00:01:03.81
Agent isolation adds one more: whatever an agent reads,

00:01:03.81 --> 00:01:09.59
no tool lets it change Hewn configuration, budgets, secrets or another project.

00:01:10.74 --> 00:01:14.96
An operator supplies a credential with the Hewn command line.

00:01:14.96 --> 00:01:18.43
Hewn secret set takes the value on standard input,

00:01:18.43 --> 00:01:22.31
so it is never in the shell's history or a process list.

00:01:22.31 --> 00:01:27.78
Asking to store anything that isn't one of Hewn's seven credentials is refused.

00:01:28.13 --> 00:01:32.87
Hewn secret list prints each credential with the time it was last set,

00:01:32.87 --> 00:01:34.01
and nothing more.

00:01:34.01 --> 00:01:39.49
Locally the store is the login keychain on macOS, or the Secret Service on Linux.

00:01:39.49 --> 00:01:43.82
The keychain entry is a generic password under the service name,

00:01:43.82 --> 00:01:46.18
with the credential as its account.

00:01:46.53 --> 00:01:48.51
The API shows the same thing.

00:01:48.51 --> 00:01:54.25
Settings slash credentials lists each name, what it is for, and when it was updated.

00:01:54.25 --> 00:01:56.43
There is no value field to fill.

00:01:56.78 --> 00:02:00.45
The secret store interface has three implementations.

00:02:00.45 --> 00:02:02.45
Azure Key Vault in the cloud.

00:02:02.45 --> 00:02:07.99
The OS key store locally, which only ever passes a value to the keychain tool on

00:02:07.99 --> 00:02:09.03
standard input.

00:02:09.03 --> 00:02:10.55
And memory, for tests.

00:02:10.55 --> 00:02:16.02
A configuration source reads each credential into the key the API already used,

00:02:16.02 --> 00:02:21.21
so nothing that reads the worker token or the GitHub App key had to change.

00:02:21.56 --> 00:02:26.34
The worker reads its own credentials the same way, from the same keychain.

00:02:26.34 --> 00:02:28.72
Its log says which it found, by name.

00:02:29.87 --> 00:02:33.37
To show redaction, a scripted run fails on purpose,

00:02:33.37 --> 00:02:37.27
with an error that holds the model key from the keychain,

00:02:37.27 --> 00:02:42.61
a GitHub token planted in a readme, and an Azure storage key read from a mock.

00:02:42.96 --> 00:02:47.63
Mission Control shows the failure with three stars where each of them was,

00:02:47.63 --> 00:02:50.41
in the failure callout and in the run's log.

00:02:50.41 --> 00:02:52.62
Here it is in dark, and on a phone.

00:02:52.97 --> 00:02:57.86
The server's JSON log line for the same failure is redacted the same way.

00:02:58.21 --> 00:03:01.28
The redaction pipeline shows every way out.

00:03:01.28 --> 00:03:05.62
Text from the worker is redacted before it leaves the worker.

00:03:05.62 --> 00:03:09.76
In the API, run log lines, pull request titles and bodies,

00:03:09.76 --> 00:03:14.46
server log entries and every event payload pass the same redactor,

00:03:14.46 --> 00:03:18.46
before the database, SignalR, GitHub or standard output.

00:03:18.81 --> 00:03:23.50
The redactor first replaces the value of every credential Hewn holds,

00:03:23.50 --> 00:03:26.91
whether it came from the store or the environment.

00:03:26.91 --> 00:03:32.01
Then the token patterns: GitHub tokens, Anthropic keys, Azure account keys,

00:03:32.01 --> 00:03:36.23
signatures and client secrets, private keys and bearer tokens.

00:03:36.23 --> 00:03:41.95
An assignment keeps its name, so token equals three stars still says what was there.

00:03:42.30 --> 00:03:46.51
Every event is redacted string by string after it is serialized,

00:03:46.51 --> 00:03:51.77
so no event type can slip past, and a pull request's title and body are redacted

00:03:51.77 --> 00:03:53.42
before they reach GitHub.

00:03:54.57 --> 00:03:59.60
The scripted run also writes git and npm credentials into its workspace,

00:03:59.60 --> 00:04:01.35
as a build's tools might.

00:04:01.35 --> 00:04:03.94
While the stage runs, they are there.

00:04:03.94 --> 00:04:06.88
When it ends, the whole workspace is gone.

00:04:07.23 --> 00:04:12.30
A run can leave a folder read only, and that used to make the deletion throw,

00:04:12.30 --> 00:04:15.53
leaving the files behind and stopping the worker.

00:04:15.53 --> 00:04:19.75
Now the worker makes the run's folders writable and tries again,

00:04:19.75 --> 00:04:23.57
and reports any credential file it still could not delete.

00:04:24.72 --> 00:04:29.80
Every stage's tools now come from one catalogue: files in the workspace,

00:04:29.80 --> 00:04:35.16
a shell in the run's container, skills, and the Magic Patterns design tools.

00:04:35.16 --> 00:04:40.59
None of them touches Hewn configuration, budgets, secrets or another project.

00:04:40.59 --> 00:04:45.67
A stage's gate denies anything else, a run's commands see no credential,

00:04:45.67 --> 00:04:48.85
and the run's proxy won't reach the Hewn API.

00:04:50.00 --> 00:04:52.67
Each slice started with a failing test.

00:04:52.67 --> 00:04:57.48
The credentials test asks for the references before the store existed,

00:04:57.48 --> 00:04:58.99
and failed to compile.

00:04:58.99 --> 00:05:03.65
It now checks that a supplied key appears only as a name and a time,

00:05:03.65 --> 00:05:07.70
and that a credential in the store is the one the API uses.

00:05:08.05 --> 00:05:13.26
The redaction test sends a log line and a failure holding every kind of secret,

00:05:13.26 --> 00:05:15.56
and opens a pull request with them.

00:05:15.56 --> 00:05:19.32
It failed with the old mask and the stored value showing.

00:05:19.32 --> 00:05:24.73
Now the stored line, the events, the server log and the pull request on GitHub all

00:05:24.73 --> 00:05:25.78
say three stars.

00:05:26.13 --> 00:05:30.82
The workspace test writes credentials, then ends runs by success,

00:05:30.82 --> 00:05:32.62
failure and a lost lease.

00:05:32.62 --> 00:05:36.30
The read only case failed with directory not empty,

00:05:36.30 --> 00:05:38.68
and the worker took no more runs.

00:05:38.68 --> 00:05:40.70
Now every workspace is gone.

00:05:41.05 --> 00:05:46.45
The agent tests check the tool catalogue, and that the worker's token opens none of

00:05:46.45 --> 00:05:49.96
the settings, budget, credential or project endpoints.

00:05:49.96 --> 00:05:53.14
Those already held; the tests keep them that way.

00:05:53.14 --> 00:05:57.50
In all, the backend has three hundred and fifty four tests passing,

00:05:57.50 --> 00:06:00.29
and the worker a hundred and seventy seven.

00:06:01.44 --> 00:06:03.72
Journey thirty seven is complete.

00:06:03.72 --> 00:06:09.09
Credentials live in Key Vault or the OS key store, supplied on standard input,

00:06:09.09 --> 00:06:11.08
and shown only as references.

00:06:11.08 --> 00:06:16.73
Every log line, event and pull request leaves with three stars where a secret was.

00:06:16.73 --> 00:06:21.62
And a run's workspace, credentials included, is gone when the run ends.

00:06:21.62 --> 00:06:23.48
Next, journey thirty eight.
